.TH GHDEB 1 "2026-08-01" "ghdeb 0.3.6" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ghdeb \- Install .deb packages from GitHub Releases
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ghdeb
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ghdeb
is a lightweight CLI tool that simplifies installing and upgrading .deb packages
directly from GitHub Releases. It handles architecture detection, asset matching,
downloading, and installation in a single command.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS install
.B ghdeb install
.IB owner / repo [ @tag ]
.PP
Install or upgrade a package to the specified version. If no tag is given,
the latest stable release is used.
.SS upgrade
.B ghdeb upgrade
.RI [ owner/repo ]
.PP
Upgrade managed packages. If no package is specified, all managed packages
are upgraded. Automatically scans for orphan packages before upgrading.
.SS scan
.B ghdeb scan
.RB [ \-\-deep ]
.PP
Scan the system for GitHub-sourced orphan packages (packages installed without
an apt source) and optionally add them to management.
.TP
.B \-\-deep
Also fetch each package's Homepage URL and try to extract a GitHub repository
link from it.
.SS list
.B ghdeb list
.RB [ \-\-refresh ]
.PP
List all managed packages, showing recorded version, system version, latest
available version, and upgrade status.
.TP
.B \-\-refresh
Force refresh the version cache by clearing all cached release data and
re-fetching from GitHub API.
.SS history
.B ghdeb history
.IB owner / repo
.PP
Show the complete operation history (install, upgrade, remove) for a package.
.SS remove
.B ghdeb remove
.IB owner / repo
.PP
Mark a package as removed. The package itself is not uninstalled; only the
ghdeb management record is marked as removed. History is preserved.
.SS set\-repo
.B ghdeb set\-repo
.I pkg
.IB owner / repo
.PP
Set the GitHub repository for a package that was previously scanned but has
no repository assigned.
.SS info
.B ghdeb info
.IB owner / repo
.PP
Show the latest release information for a repository, including matched
download assets for the current architecture.
.SS version
.B ghdeb version
.PP
Print the ghdeb version.
.SH ARCHITECTURE MATCHING
.B ghdeb
automatically detects the system architecture via
.B dpkg \-\-print\-architecture
and matches release assets by filename patterns:
.TS
tab(@);
l l.
System Arch@Matched Keywords
amd64@amd64, x86_64, x86-64, x64
arm64@arm64, aarch64
armhf@armhf, armv7l, armv7
i386@i386, x86, i686, 386
.TE
.SH CACHE
.B ghdeb
caches release information in
.B ~/.cache/ghdeb/releases.json
with a 24-hour TTL. Downloaded .deb files are cached in
.BR ~/.cache/ghdeb/ .
.SH STATE
Managed package records are stored in
.BR ~/.local/state/ghdeb/installed.json .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GITHUB_TOKEN
.TQ
.B GH_TOKEN
GitHub personal access token. Increases API rate limit from 60 requests/hour
(unauthenticated) to 5,000 requests/hour.
.SH LOCALE
Output language is determined by the
.B LANG
environment variable. Chinese (zh_*) produces Chinese output; all other
locales produce English output.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.cache/ghdeb/releases.json
Release version cache (24h TTL).
.TP
.B ~/.cache/ghdeb/*.deb
Downloaded .deb package cache.
.TP
.B ~/.local/state/ghdeb/installed.json
Managed package state records.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Error (invalid arguments, network failure, install failure, etc.).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B ghdeb install sharkdp/bat
Install the latest version of bat.
.TP
.B ghdeb install sharkdp/bat@v0.25.0
Install a specific version of bat.
.TP
.B ghdeb upgrade
Upgrade all managed packages.
.TP
.B ghdeb upgrade sharkdp/bat
Upgrade only bat.
.TP
.B ghdeb scan --deep
Scan for orphan packages, fetching Homepages for GitHub links.
.TP
.B ghdeb list --refresh
List all packages, forcing a fresh check of latest versions.
.TP
.B ghdeb set\-repo draw.io jgraph/drawio
Assign a GitHub repo to a previously scanned package.
Configuration file (JSON format):
.TP
.B ~/.config/ghdeb/config.json
User configuration file. Currently supports:
.RS
.TP
.B proxy
Proxy URL (e.g., "http://wpad.lan:8888"). Used when environment variables
are not set.
.RE
.PP
Example config.json:
.EX
{
  "proxy": "http://wpad.lan:8888"
}
.EE

.SH SHELL COMPLETION
.B ghdeb
provides shell completion scripts for bash and zsh. After installation,
completions are automatically available for new shells. For existing shells:
.PP
.B bash:
source /usr/share/bash-completion/completions/ghdeb
.br
or restart your shell.
.PP
.B zsh:
run
.I compinit
or restart your shell. Completions are installed to
.IR /usr/share/zsh/site-functions/_ghdeb .
.PP
Completion features:
.TP
.B Command completion
Type
.I ghdeb
and press Tab to see available commands.
.TP
.B Package completion
For commands that take package names (upgrade, history, remove, set-repo),
press Tab to see managed packages from your ghdeb state.
.TP
.B Option completion
Type
.I ghdeb scan --
or
.I ghdeb list --
and press Tab to see available options.

